        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "a2c27ea4-f5cf-3952-9c31-72a12eda004f",
                "word": "pandéisme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0b403a8f-5c3e-41c4-9ab9-b1f52e28eb13",
                        "entry_id": "a2c27ea4-f5cf-3952-9c31-72a12eda004f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pandéismes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2cee747b-4a0e-3777-95fd-5082e8fa9476",
                        "entry_id": "a2c27ea4-f5cf-3952-9c31-72a12eda004f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Système philosophique suivant lequel on affirme l’identité substantielle de Dieu et du monde et on n’admet d’autre Dieu qu’une substance infinie dont tous les êtres sont des modes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1142362-fb48-4a0c-a0dd-df45b54c4023",
                                "sense_id": "2cee747b-4a0e-3777-95fd-5082e8fa9476",
                                "text": "Ok je continue. Aujourd'hui notre sujet n'est pas le pandéisme ou l'apathéisme, mais l'athéisme et ses formes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "354f378b-cb83-4cfb-b482-3ffbee7307f0",
                        "source_entry_id": "a2c27ea4-f5cf-3952-9c31-72a12eda004f",
                        "source_sense_id": "2cee747b-4a0e-3777-95fd-5082e8fa9476",
                        "target_lang_word": "Pandeismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Pandeismus",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ed19864-4310-301c-80ae-0d84d1de40b3",
                                        "entry_id": "26d05446-be5e-3530-a3c7-893ec0ce874e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "eine Synthese von Elementen des Pantheismus und des Deismus, konkret: der Glaube daran, dass Gott das Universum erschaffen hat, und zur gleichen Zeit, dass das Universum jetzt das Ganze dieses Gottes ist; deshalb kann dieser Gott auch in keiner Weise mehr auf die Welt einwirken"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Theologie"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6023c35-5de4-4d84-aff8-6bc186d5cc62",
                                                "sense_id": "4ed19864-4310-301c-80ae-0d84d1de40b3",
                                                "text": "„Wenn auch nur durch einen Buchstaben (d statt th), unterscheiden wir grundsätzlich Pandeismus vom Pantheismus.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d55731db-b164-4459-8e27-0fca5fa37ceb",
                                                "sense_id": "4ed19864-4310-301c-80ae-0d84d1de40b3",
                                                "text": "„Pantheismus und Pandeismus, Monismus und Dualismus: alles dies sind in Wirklichkeit nur verschiedene Formen des Gottschauens, verschiedene Beleuchtungsarten des Grundbegriffes, nämlich des Höchsten, von dem aus die verschiedenen Strahlungen in die Menschenseele sich hinein senken und hier ein Spiegelbild projizieren […]“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "320be1fb-fb58-4951-81f6-dfd7db38bbe1",
                                                "sense_id": "4ed19864-4310-301c-80ae-0d84d1de40b3",
                                                "text": "„[…] der zweite Hauptteil bespricht die philosophisch-deistischen und theosophischen Anschauungen vom Pandeismus der alten Ägypter und Inder bis zu Leibnizens prästabilierter Harmonie und Herbarts Realen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab9170b5-10a2-4f48-b039-fd26f8f6eec6",
                                                "sense_id": "4ed19864-4310-301c-80ae-0d84d1de40b3",
                                                "text": "„Mochten die Muslime in der großen Stadt auch ihre geschlossenen kleinen Welten aufbauen, kam es doch immer wieder zu Reibungen mit der hinduistischen Mehrheitsgesellschaft: Kastensystem vs. Egalität der Muslime, Fleischverzehr der Muslime vs. Vegetarismus der Hindus, Monotheismus der Muslime vs. Pandeismus und Heiligenverehrung unter den Hindus.\""
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7f55ca84-9cc8-4e00-a864-bc3efede1bf0",
                        "source_entry_id": "a2c27ea4-f5cf-3952-9c31-72a12eda004f",
                        "source_sense_id": "2cee747b-4a0e-3777-95fd-5082e8fa9476",
                        "target_lang_word": "pandeism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pandeism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a69eb2e-f1b5-3284-84d1-66d234c3d97d",
                                        "entry_id": "df38ade3-60d2-3748-b8eb-7d64b818380c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A belief in a god who is both pantheistic and deistic, in particular a god who designed the universe and then became it and ceased to exist separately and act consciously with respect to it."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9719193b-13b3-4883-9c56-c827f7913e50",
                                                "sense_id": "1a69eb2e-f1b5-3284-84d1-66d234c3d97d",
                                                "text": "Just as [absolute perfection in some respects, relative perfection in all others] is the whole positive content of perfection, so CW, or the conception of the Creator-and-the-Whole-of-what-he-has-created as constituting one life, the super-whole which in its everlasting essence is uncreated (and does not necessitate just the parts which the whole has) but in its de facto concreteness is created – this panentheistic doctrine contains all of deism and pandeism except their arbitrary negations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3095d4e0-c745-4970-9f50-c4c915fbebdf",
                                                "sense_id": "1a69eb2e-f1b5-3284-84d1-66d234c3d97d",
                                                "text": "What appeared here, at the center of the Pythagorean tradition in philosophy, is another view of psyche that seems to owe little or nothing to the pan-vitalism or pan-deism (see theion) that is the legacy of the Milesians."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91891059-c80c-49a8-a79d-ecfcf348a04b",
                                                "sense_id": "1a69eb2e-f1b5-3284-84d1-66d234c3d97d",
                                                "text": "All the actions of created intelligences are not merely the actions of God. Creatures act freely and responsibly as the proximate causes of their own moral actions. If God was the proximate cause of every act, all things would simply be “God in motion”. That is nothing less than pantheism, or more exactly, pandeism. The Creator is distinct from his creation. The reality of secondary causes is what separates Christian theism from pandeism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0f5dd2e-475e-4840-b27a-3a70bbc03b0c",
                                                "sense_id": "1a69eb2e-f1b5-3284-84d1-66d234c3d97d",
                                                "text": "It could also be argued that the god that no longer requires interaction with the creation is superior to the one that does, so that deistic concepts, including pandeism, are again preferable. Similarly, concerning experiential arguments, the 'hidden' and possibly 'indifferent' god of pandeism better explains why so many people do not experience god, internally, yet also can explain why some do. Pandeisms, and other pantheisms, particularly polytheistic forms, also better explain why it is not only the god of theism (and specifically, Christian theism) that is internally experienced by some people."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb8f9efe-569b-3dea-928c-9efe0ac31061",
                                        "entry_id": "df38ade3-60d2-3748-b8eb-7d64b818380c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Worship which admits or tolerates favourable aspects of all religions; omnitheism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rare",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66ee3d98-898f-4686-b32c-56fb0b579e1f",
                                                "sense_id": "bb8f9efe-569b-3dea-928c-9efe0ac31061",
                                                "text": "We hear men prophesy that this war means the death of Christianity and an era of Pandeism or perhaps even the destruction of all which we call modern civilization and culture. We hear men predict that the ultimate result of the war will be a blessing to humanity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eed68bc8-3061-4d7b-8e2c-afac1585eddf",
                                                "sense_id": "bb8f9efe-569b-3dea-928c-9efe0ac31061",
                                                "text": "I first came across this extension of ecumenism into pan-deism among some Roman Catholic scholars interested primarily in the \"reunion of the churches,\" [...] Thus they do not necessarily discern in Rome's ecumenism and pan-deism a project for world domination. Yet this danger certainly exists."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa7cfc5f-395b-47d4-846e-0a42e4649907",
                                                "sense_id": "bb8f9efe-569b-3dea-928c-9efe0ac31061",
                                                "text": "If the Bible is only human lore, and not divine truth, then we have no real answer to those who say, \"Let's pick the best out of all religions and blend it all into Pan-Deism – one world religion with one god made out of many\"."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d2e4e95-2557-4175-a1e5-b9375209e310",
                        "source_entry_id": "a2c27ea4-f5cf-3952-9c31-72a12eda004f",
                        "source_sense_id": "2cee747b-4a0e-3777-95fd-5082e8fa9476",
